      <activity id="b5e5c376-a1a1-503b-90fd-49c0c966475b" activityNameId="4baa1f1e-2769-5c52-855d-df0d9c0fefdc" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Crude oil, production US, at long distance transport</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Crude oil, production US, at long distance transport
Calculation for transport distances assuming transport by pipeline offshore and onshore as well as sea transport in tanker. Sites and modes of transportation based on the supply situation in 2016.;
UUID: 4084a1e3-3c04-32fe-9804-52164553ab67
Transportation of crude oil from exploration site to refinery at seaport in Central Europe (FR, BE, GE or NL). Includes transport service requirements and emissions from oil handling and evaporation.
Location: Calculations based on assumptions for supply to European refineries.
Technology: Operation of crude oil pipelines by electricity.
Time period: Transport modes investigated for 2016
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature. Online calculators for distances. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_4084a1e3-3c04-32fe-9804-52164553ab67.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
